{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XtPnn5Q86Gvs3gAQySAtpy","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n     2→title: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n     6→  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n     7→  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n     8→  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n     9→\n    10→actor: Human Operator\n    11→\n    12→trigger: |\n    13→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n    14→  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n    15→\n    16→flow:\n    17→  - id: F1\n    18→    step: |\n    19→      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n    20→      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n    21→      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n    25→      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n    29→  - id: F4\n    30→    step: |\n    31→      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n    32→      and exits 2.\n    33→  - id: F5\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n    36→      no warnings or errors.\n    37→  - id: F6\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n    40→      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n    41→  - id: F7\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n    44→\n    45→touchpoints:\n    46→  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n    47→  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n    48→  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n    49→\n    50→success_criteria:\n    51→  - id: S1\n    52→    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n    53→  - id: S2\n    54→    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n    55→  - id: S3\n    56→    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    57→  - id: S4\n    58→    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n    59→  - id: S5\n    60→    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n    61→  - id: S6\n    62→    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    63→  - id: S7\n    64→    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n    65→\n    66→out_of_scope:\n    67→  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n    68→  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n    69→  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n    70→\n    71→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    72→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ec44b0e-995a-4ca7-b2ad-70942cb22054","uuid":"fbc7dd1b-53f1-4f3c-99f7-a0d8c2eff60a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/199/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc001-magefiles.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\ntitle: \"Build, lint, and version-check via mage targets\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs mage build to compile cmd/version to bin/version, verifies that the\n  binary prints the repository's version tag, runs mage lint to confirm no warnings, and\n  runs mage clean to remove build artifacts. This exercises the full build lifecycle\n  specified in prd011-magefiles before any utility code exists.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd011-magefiles.yaml) and wants to verify that the\n  build pipeline produces a working binary.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage build. The target compiles every package under cmd/ to bin/.\n      For cmd/version, the target resolves the latest version tag via\n      git describe --tags --abbrev=0 --match \"v[0-9]*\" and passes it through -ldflags.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version. The binary prints the version tag (e.g., \"v0.20260228.0\")\n      to stdout followed by a newline and exits 0.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --version. The output is identical to F2.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The operator runs bin/version --bogus. The binary prints a usage message to stderr\n      and exits 2.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage lint. golangci-lint runs on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/ with\n      no warnings or errors.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The operator runs mage clean. The bin/ directory and its contents are removed. If\n      bin/ does not exist, the target succeeds silently.\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The operator verifies that bin/ no longer exists after mage clean.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/version — version string printing, ldflags injection (prd011-magefiles R1)\"\n  - T2: \"magefiles/ — build, lint, clean targets (prd011-magefiles R2, R3, R4)\"\n  - T3: \"configuration.yaml — project.binary_dir, project.go_source_dirs (prd011-magefiles R6)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: mage build succeeds and bin/version exists.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: bin/version prints a version tag matching v[0-9]* and exits 0.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: bin/version --bogus prints to stderr and exits 2.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: mage lint passes with no warnings on cmd/, pkg/, and magefiles/.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: mage clean removes bin/ and succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: A development build (no ldflags) produces a binary that prints \"dev\".\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Differential testing of cmd/version against a reference binary (there is no GNU version equivalent).\n  - mage install is exercised by the operator manually; it is not part of this use case's primary flow.\n  - Orchestrator, generator, scaffold, and prompt targets are provided by cobbler-scaffold and not covered here.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0193Ydn7Z8xtB1GhUZazXymY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of what cmd/version needs to do:\n\n1. **Package**: `cmd/version/`, compiles to standalone binary\n2. **Version variable**: Set via `-ldflags \"-X main.version=<tag>\"`, defaults to \"dev\" if not set\n3. **No arguments**: Print version string to stdout followed by newline, exit 0\n4. **`--version` or `-v`**: Same output as no-argument invocation\n5. **Any other flag**: Print usage message to stderr and exit 2\n6. **Export**: Must export a variable or function so other cmd/ packages can import the version string (R1.5)\n\n\n7. **Constraint**: Since this is `package main`, it can't be imported by other packages in Go - there's a fundamental conflict between the requirement to be importable and the cmd/ convention of using `package main`. The task specifies creating `cmd/version/main.go`, so I'll proceed with the main package structure and note this limitation. and the conventions say \"package main\". R1.5 might be a future concern that would require creating a separate package, but the task says to implement exactly what's specified without adding extra. Given that the task says D2: \"Implement exactly what the PRD specifies -- do not add features, flags, or output fields not in the PRD\", I should implement cmd/version/main.go as package main with the version variable.\n\nFor R1.5, the way to handle this in Go would typically be to have a separate `pkg/version` or `internal/version` package. But since I'm only allowed to create `cmd/version/main.go`, and the design says \"do not deviate from the specified files unless a requirement makes it necessary\", I'll implement the `main` package with a `version` variable that gets set via ldflags. The export requirement can be addressed through comments noting that other binaries would use the same ldflags mechanism.\n\nSince it's package main, the version variable can't be imported anyway, so R1.5 is likely aspirational for a future refactor. I'll follow the existing patterns from cmd/cat and cmd/wc: copyright header, package main, progName constant, signal handler, manual flag parsing, and a version variable controlled by ldflags with buffered stdout.\n\nNow for the flag behavior: no arguments or `--version`/`-v` prints the version and exits 0, while any other flag triggers a usage message to stderr and exits 2. The `--` pattern from cmd/cat stops flag parsing, but since cmd/version doesn't take file arguments, it's less relevant here. I need to follow the PRD strictly where \"any other flag\" causes an exit 2 with usage output.\n\nWriting the implementation now... Writing the flag handling logic...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3694,"cache_read_input_tokens":46396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3694},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3ec44b0e-995a-4ca7-b2ad-70942cb22054","uuid":"61085a4a-57d6-4ced-9ef5-dff089d89d29"}
